<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES - Tenders total A$150 mln.</title>
<headline>RTRS-AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES - Tenders total A$150 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian promissory note issuers greeted the new week with six tenders totalling A$150.0 million in value, the biggest one-day total since August.</p>
<p>Dealers said rollovers accounted for most of the issuance.</p>
<p>CS First Boston made the largest issue on the day, selling A$50 million of its early January-dated paper at about seven basis points over the mid-rate for corresponding bank bills.</p>
<p>The bill curve has strengthened over the morning but turnover remains slight. At 0023 GMT (11.23 a.m.) March 1997 bank bill futures were up 0.09 to 93.75.</p>
